From: FIocker <4461558+FIocker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 16:10:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] shader_library: fix the #4343 review findings; recount
 with llvm-mc 21 and 23

Review findings on #4343 (@tupacfan04):
* A compute record may hold NONE in any field (ref allows it), but parse()
  indexed the blob table with a NONE layout (IndexError) and main() decoded a
  NONE state. A record without a program now names no stage, one without a
  layout links no digest, one without a state gets no dispatch fields, and
  library.json gives a missing program as null.
* find_library inflated any false zlib header without a cap, up to ~132 MB per
  stream. Each stream now inflates to at most BLOCK + 1 bytes (a library block
  is at most 64 KiB, so a longer stream isn't one), and a header that asks for
  more than 1032:1 of the bytes after it is rejected.
Three new tests fail on main (the IndexError, the ratio, a too-long stream with a
library header) and pass here.

docs/shader_library.md:
* 91 compute programs set TG_SIZE_EN, not 90 (90 was the refusal count; one
  program is refused earlier).
* A default run writes 21,521 programs: --stages all adds the slot-6 one
  (@bielfreedom).
* Section 5 said llvm-mc 23, but those counts were made with 21.1.8, which can't
  decode the vcc tuples (LLVM 23 added VCCTuple). The section now compares 21.1.8
  (15,551), 23.1.5 (16,699) and 23.1.5 with #6446, #6808 and #6809 (18,544) at
  main 561b65a8, and lists what stops the rest. Section 4 says to use llvm-mc 23.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
